/docs/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/

# The built dashboard, produced by scripts/build_ui.py. It is packaged into the wheel and
# the sdist as a build artifact (see pyproject.toml) rather than committed, because a
# checked-in bundle goes stale against the source it was built from without saying so.
/src/mlexperimenttracker/server/static/

# The static demo's recorded API responses live at ml_frontend/src/demo/snapshot.json and
# are deliberately NOT ignored, even though they are generated. Rollup resolves that import
# while building the normal bundle — it drops the module afterwards, but it must be able to
# read it first — so ignoring the path breaks `npm run build` on a fresh clone, and the
# normal build is the one that ships in the wheel.
#
# What is committed there is an empty placeholder, not a capture: no runs, no metrics,
# `"source": "not captured yet"`. So the objection that a committed capture keeps answering
# for an API that no longer exists does not apply — there is nothing in it to go stale.
# scripts/build_demo_snapshot.py overwrites it locally and in the Render build; the
# resulting ~540 KiB file is a build artifact and is not meant to be committed.

